From 197eb0c305d0aae9fbaa1700c3a8c0db70149059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:27:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 45/63] native: beside GLM's host tier, a device prompt cache
 under one state goes to the KV pages

Production (4 bpw, fp8 pages, reserve 3.5, --context 864,256, 4 streams) left the device prompt cache 0.176 GiB, under
the 0.215 GiB of the smallest state (2,048 tokens), and warned at every start that the cache "cannot keep one state",
though the 8 GiB pinned host tier a rank kept them all along: the warning priced the card's share alone.

- A family that keeps states past the card (snap_host_tier: GLM) no longer funds a device share that holds no state
  of its own: the plan gives it to the KV pages (Plan.skipped) and the store keeps states in the host tier alone. At
  production's shape the pool grows from 1,692 to 1,749 pages (866,304 to 895,488 tokens) and the store's budget from
  8.18 to 8.0 GiB a rank. A share that holds one state stays on the card; other families are unchanged; a cache
  turned off (--prompt-cache-gib 0, --keep 0) skips nothing and makes no store, as before.
- The startup warning and the prompt_cache_* metrics read the store's real budget (storeBudget: the card's share and
  the host tier), so production's 0.18 + 8.0 GiB is quiet; a card's share alone under one state still warns.
- The startup line says where the states went: ", the prompt cache in pinned host memory alone (the 0.18 GiB the card
  had left it holds no state: the KV pages took it)".

Why the pages and not the card (measured on this machine, both GPUs, another engine running): a 180 MiB slice of a
kept state restores device-to-device in 0.29 ms and from pinned host pages in 7.9 ms (22 GiB/s), in the 2 MiB copies
cuda_snapshot_pages.move issues; so the 0.18 GiB device share saves at most ~7.6 ms on one restore of the one state
that sits on it (a 125K hit's TTFT is ~480 ms), against 57 pages (29,184 tokens) more for every stream. The KV pool
was exactly one --context window plus 3 pages, so a request near the cap left no room beside it.

Test (kv merge): production's shape gives 1,692 pages and a 0.176 GiB share without the rule, 1,749 pages and the
host tier alone with it; storeBudget is 8 GiB then (0 with the cache off, share + host without the rule); the
warning is quiet for both, loud for the share alone; a share of one state, or a family without a host tier, keeps it.

